# Tessl consumer-side install state — everything `tessl install` GENERATES.
# The manifest that drives it, `tessl.json`, is committed: it is this repo's
# package.json, and `.tessl/` below is the resolved cache it fills, the
# node_modules. `.tesslignore` keeps both out of the published plugin, which
# ships from .tessl-plugin/plugin.json.
.tessl/
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.gemini/
.mcp.json
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
